{"id":"mahabharata-5-180","work":"mahabharata","part":5,"partName":"उद्योगपर्व","partNameEn":"Udyoga Parva","unit":180,"title":"अशीत्यधिकशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 180 · The first day's battle","summary":{"en":"Parashurama and Bhishma fight fiercely through the first day, wounding each other with showers of arrows. When the sun sets, the battle is halted.","kn":"ಪರಶುರಾಮ ಭೀಷ್ಮರು ಮೊದಲ ದಿನವಿಡೀ ಬಾಣಮಳೆಯಿಂದ ಪರಸ್ಪರ ಗಾಯಗೊಳಿಸುತ್ತಾ ಭೀಕರವಾಗಿ ಹೋರಾಡುತ್ತಾರೆ. ಸೂರ್ಯಾಸ್ತವಾದಾಗ ಯುದ್ಧ ನಿಲ್ಲುತ್ತದೆ.","hi":"परशुराम और भीष्म पहले दिन भर भयंकर युद्ध करते हैं और बाणों की वर्षा से एक-दूसरे को घायल करते हैं। सूर्यास्त होने पर युद्ध रोक दिया जाता है।","te":"పరశురాముడు, భీష్ముడు మొదటి రోజంతా బాణవర్షాలతో ఒకరినొకరు గాయపరచుకుంటూ భీకరంగా పోరాడతారు. సూర్యాస్తమయం కాగానే యుద్ధం ఆగుతుంది.","ta":"பரஶுராமரும் பீஷ்மரும் முதல் நாள் முழுவதும் அம்பு மழையால் ஒருவரையொருவர் காயப்படுத்தியபடி கடுமையாகப் போரிடுகிறார்கள். சூரியன் மறைந்ததும் போர் நிறுத்தப்படுகிறது.","ml":"പരശുരാമനും ഭീഷ്മരും ആദ്യദിവസം മുഴുവൻ ഘോരമായി പൊരുതുന്നു; അമ്പുമഴ പെയ്ത് പരസ്പരം മുറിവേൽപ്പിക്കുന്നു. സൂര്യൻ അസ്തമിക്കുമ്പോൾ യുദ്ധം നിർത്തിവെക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 5.180; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Jan 23 2024","sections":[{"title":"अम्बोपाख्यानपर्व","titleEn":"Ambopakhyana Parva (The story of Amba)","verses":[{"text":"भीष्म उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"तमहं स्मयन्निव रणे प्रत्यभाषं व्यवस्थितम् ।\nभूमिष्ठं नोत्सहे योद्धुं भवन्तं रथमास्थितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As if smiling, I answered him as he stood in the battlefield: I cannot fight you standing on the ground while I am on a chariot."}},{"n":2,"text":"आरोह स्यन्दनं वीर कवचं च महाभुज ।\nबधान समरे राम यदि योद्धुं मयेच्छसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Mount a chariot, hero, and put on armor, mighty-armed Rama, if you wish to fight me in the battle."}},{"n":3,"text":"ततो मामब्रवीद्रामः स्मयमानो रणाजिरे ।\nरथो मे मेदिनी भीष्म वाहा वेदाः सदश्ववत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Rama, smiling on the field, said to me: The earth is my chariot, Bhishma; the Vedas are my fine horses."}},{"n":4,"text":"सूतो मे मातरिश्वा वै कवचं वेदमातरः ।\nसुसंवीतो रणे ताभिर्योत्स्येऽहं कुरुनन्दन ॥","meaning":{"en":"The wind is my charioteer, and the mothers of the Vedas are my armor; well wrapped in them I will fight, joy of the Kurus."}},{"n":5,"text":"एवं ब्रुवाणो गान्धारे रामो मां सत्यविक्रमः ।\nशरव्रातेन महता सर्वतः पर्यवारयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As he spoke thus, son of Gandhari, Rama of true valor surrounded me on all sides with a great flood of arrows."}},{"n":6,"text":"ततोऽपश्यं जामदग्न्यं रथे दिव्ये व्यवस्थितम् ।\nसर्वायुधधरे श्रीमत्यद्भुतोपमदर्शने ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then I saw Jamadagni's son standing in a divine chariot, bearing all weapons, splendid, wondrous to see."}},{"n":7,"text":"मनसा विहिते पुण्ये विस्तीर्णे नगरोपमे ।\nदिव्याश्वयुजि संनद्धे काञ्चनेन विभूषिते ॥","meaning":{"en":"It was made by thought, holy and vast like a city, yoked with divine horses, armored and adorned with gold."}},{"n":8,"text":"ध्वजेन च महाबाहो सोमालंकृतलक्ष्मणा ।\nधनुर्धरो बद्धतूणो बद्धगोधाङ्गुलित्रवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Its banner, mighty-armed one, bore the mark of the moon; he held his bow, wore his quiver and had on his lizard-skin finger guards."}},{"n":9,"text":"सारथ्यं कृतवांस्तत्र युयुत्सोरकृतव्रणः ।\nसखा वेदविदत्यन्तं दयितो भार्गवस्य ह ॥","meaning":{"en":"Akritavrana, a friend deeply dear to the Bhargava and a knower of the Veda, acted as his charioteer for the fighter."}},{"n":10,"text":"आह्वयानः स मां युद्धे मनो हर्षयतीव मे ।\nपुनः पुनरभिक्रोशन्नभियाहीति भार्गवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Challenging me to battle he seemed to gladden my mind, the Bhargava shouting again and again, \"Come on!\""}},{"n":11,"text":"तमादित्यमिवोद्यन्तमनाधृष्यं महाबलम् ।\nक्षत्रियान्तकरं राममेकमेकः समासदम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"I, alone, faced that Rama, destroyer of Kshatriyas, alone, mighty and unassailable, rising like the sun."}},{"n":12,"text":"ततोऽहं बाणपातेषु त्रिषु वाहान्निगृह्य वै ।\nअवतीर्य धनुर्न्यस्य पदातिरृषिसत्तमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, after checking my horses at three arrow-flights, I got down, laid aside my bow, and went on foot to the best of sages."}},{"n":13,"text":"अभ्यगच्छं तदा राममर्चिष्यन्द्विजसत्तमम् ।\nअभिवाद्य चैनं विधिवदब्रुवं वाक्यमुत्तमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"I went to honor Rama, the best of the twice-born, saluted him duly and spoke excellent words."}},{"n":14,"text":"योत्स्ये त्वया रणे राम विशिष्टेनाधिकेन च ।\nगुरुणा धर्मशीलेन जयमाशास्स्व मे विभो ॥","meaning":{"en":"I will fight you in battle, Rama, a better and greater man, my teacher and righteous; wish me victory, lord."}},{"text":"राम उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Rama said:"}},{"n":15,"text":"एवमेतत्कुरुश्रेष्ठ कर्तव्यं भूतिमिच्छता ।\nधर्मो ह्येष महाबाहो विशिष्टैः सह युध्यताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"This is how it should be, best of Kurus, for one who wants prosperity; this is dharma, mighty-armed one, for those who fight their betters."}},{"n":16,"text":"शपेयं त्वां न चेदेवमागच्छेथा विशां पते ।\nयुध्यस्व त्वं रणे यत्तो धैर्यमालम्ब्य कौरव ॥","meaning":{"en":"I would have cursed you, lord of the people, if you had not come so. Fight, then, in battle, alert, holding to courage, Kaurava."}},{"n":17,"text":"न तु ते जयमाशासे त्वां हि जेतुमहं स्थितः ।\nगच्छ युध्यस्व धर्मेण प्रीतोऽस्मि चरितेन ते ॥","meaning":{"en":"But I do not wish you victory, for I have come to defeat you; go, fight by dharma; I am pleased with your conduct."}},{"text":"भीष्म उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma said:"}},{"n":18,"text":"ततोऽहं तं नमस्कृत्य रथमारुह्य सत्वरः ।\nप्राध्मापयं रणे शङ्खं पुनर्हेमविभूषितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then I bowed to him, quickly mounted the chariot, and again blew my gold-adorned conch in the battle."}},{"n":19,"text":"ततो युद्धं समभवन्मम तस्य च भारत ।\nदिवसान्सुबहून्राजन्परस्परजिगीषया ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then there was a fight between me and him, Bharata, for very many days, king, each wishing to defeat the other."}},{"n":20,"text":"स मे तस्मिन्रणे पूर्वं प्राहरत्कङ्कपत्रिभिः ।\nषष्ट्या शतैश्च नवभिः शराणामग्निवर्चसाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"First in that battle he struck me with nine hundred and sixty arrows of fire-like brilliance, fletched with heron feathers."}},{"n":21,"text":"चत्वारस्तेन मे वाहाः सूतश्चैव विशां पते ।\nप्रतिरुद्धास्तथैवाहं समरे दंशितः स्थितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Four of my horses and my charioteer were stopped by him, lord of the people, but I stood armored in the battle."}},{"n":22,"text":"नमस्कृत्य च देवेभ्यो ब्राह्मणेभ्यश्च भारत ।\nतमहं स्मयन्निव रणे प्रत्यभाषं व्यवस्थितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having bowed to the gods and Brahmins, Bharata, I again answered him as he stood in battle, as if smiling."}},{"n":23,"text":"आचार्यता मानिता मे निर्मर्यादे ह्यपि त्वयि ।\nभूयस्तु शृणु मे ब्रह्मन्संपदं धर्मसंग्रहे ॥","meaning":{"en":"I honored you as my teacher even though you overstepped limits; now hear again, Brahmin, my account in the holding of dharma."}},{"n":24,"text":"ये ते वेदाः शरीरस्था ब्राह्मण्यं यच्च ते महत् ।\nतपश्च सुमहत्तप्तं न तेभ्यः प्रहराम्यहम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Vedas that live in your body, your Brahminhood and the great austerity you have practiced, against these I do not strike."}},{"n":25,"text":"प्रहरे क्षत्रधर्मस्य यं त्वं राम समास्थितः ।\nब्राह्मणः क्षत्रियत्वं हि याति शस्त्रसमुद्यमात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"I strike at the Kshatriya duty you have taken on, Rama; for a Brahmin who takes up weapons becomes a Kshatriya."}},{"n":26,"text":"पश्य मे धनुषो वीर्यं पश्य बाह्वोर्बलं च मे ।\nएष ते कार्मुकं वीर द्विधा कुर्मि ससायकम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"See the power of my bow, see the strength of my arms; hero, I will now cut your bow in two with its arrow."}},{"n":27,"text":"तस्याहं निशितं भल्लं प्राहिण्वं भरतर्षभ ।\nतेनास्य धनुषः कोटिश्छिन्ना भूमिमथागमत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"I sent a sharp broad-headed arrow at it, best of Bharatas; by it the tip of his bow was cut off and fell to the ground."}},{"n":28,"text":"नव चापि पृषत्कानां शतानि नतपर्वणाम् ।\nप्राहिण्वं कङ्कपत्राणां जामदग्न्यरथं प्रति ॥","meaning":{"en":"And I sent nine hundred straight-jointed arrows with heron feathers at Jamadagni's son's chariot."}},{"n":29,"text":"काये विषक्तास्तु तदा वायुनाभिसमीरिताः ।\nचेलुः क्षरन्तो रुधिरं नागा इव च ते शराः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Stuck in his body and driven by the wind, those arrows moved, streaming blood like snakes."}},{"n":30,"text":"क्षतजोक्षितसर्वाङ्गः क्षरन्स रुधिरं व्रणैः ।\nबभौ रामस्तदा राजन्मेरुर्धातूनिवोत्सृजन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"His whole body drenched with blood, bleeding from his wounds, Rama then shone, king, like Meru shedding its minerals."}},{"n":31,"text":"हेमन्तान्तेऽशोक इव रक्तस्तबकमण्डितः ।\nबभौ रामस्तदा राजन्क्वचित्किंशुकसंनिभः ॥","meaning":{"en":"At the end of winter, like an ashoka covered with red clusters, Rama shone, king, like a kimshuka tree in places."}},{"n":32,"text":"ततोऽन्यद्धनुरादाय रामः क्रोधसमन्वितः ।\nहेमपुङ्खान्सुनिशिताञ्शरांस्तान्हि ववर्ष सः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Rama, angry, took another bow and rained down well-sharpened gold-feathered arrows."}},{"n":33,"text":"ते समासाद्य मां रौद्रा बहुधा मर्मभेदिनः ।\nअकम्पयन्महावेगाः सर्पानलविषोपमाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Reaching me, those terrible, fast arrows, piercing vital points in many ways, shook me, like snakes, fire and poison."}},{"n":34,"text":"ततोऽहं समवष्टभ्य पुनरात्मानमाहवे ।\nशतसंख्यैः शरैः क्रुद्धस्तदा राममवाकिरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then I steadied myself again in the battle and in anger covered Rama with hundreds of arrows."}},{"n":35,"text":"स तैरग्न्यर्कसंकाशैः शरैराशीविषोपमैः ।\nशितैरभ्यर्दितो रामो मन्दचेता इवाभवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Afflicted by those sharp arrows, bright as fire and sun and like venomous snakes, Rama became as if dazed."}},{"n":36,"text":"ततोऽहं कृपयाविष्टो विनिन्द्यात्मानमात्मना ।\nधिग्धिगित्यब्रुवं युद्धं क्षत्रं च भरतर्षभ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, filled with pity, I blamed myself and said, \"Shame, shame on war and on the Kshatriya way,\" best of Bharatas."}},{"n":37,"text":"असकृच्चाब्रुवं राजञ्शोकवेगपरिप्लुतः ।\nअहो बत कृतं पापं मयेदं क्षत्रकर्मणा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Overcome with a rush of grief, I said again and again, king: Alas, this sin has been done by me through a Kshatriya's work,"}},{"n":38,"text":"गुरुर्द्विजातिर्धर्मात्मा यदेवं पीडितः शरैः ।\nततो न प्राहरं भूयो जामदग्न्याय भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"That a teacher, a Brahmin and righteous soul, is so pained by my arrows. So I did not strike Jamadagni's son again, Bharata."}},{"n":39,"text":"अथावताप्य पृथिवीं पूषा दिवससंक्षये ।\nजगामास्तं सहस्रांशुस्ततो युद्धमुपारमत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the sun, after heating the earth, went down at the day's end, and the battle stopped."}}]}]}